{"step_index":29,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-18T05:22:53Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-18T13:22:53+08:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-18T13:22:53+08:00\nShowing lines 1190-1276 of 1276\n1190:                     \"V5_Marshal_\", \"V5_FieldMasts\", \"V5_Hangar_\",\r\n1191:                     \"V5_Gantry\", \"V5_StartLight\"),\r\n1192:     \"V5_07_Lighting\": (\"LGT_V5\",),\r\n1193: }\r\n1194: \r\n1195: # 13a. 原点归位：只处理\"网格烘焙在世界坐标里\"的对象（location/rotation 为 0、scale 为 1）。\r\n1196: #      box()/球体等本来就以自身中心为原点（location 已是世界位置），不动。\r\n1197: #      注意：新建对象在 depsgraph 更新前 matrix_world 是单位阵——旧版就是读了它，\r\n1198: #      把 441 个 box 对象的 location 改成了 (0,0,0)，全堆在世界原点。这里先 update，\r\n1199: #      并且只用 matrix_basis（不依赖 depsgraph）判断。\r\n1200: bpy.context.view_layer.update()\r\n1201: _moved = 0\r\n1202: _I4 = Matrix.Identity(4)\r\n1203: for _ob in list(bpy.data.objects):\r\n1204:     if _ob.type != 'MESH' or not _ob.name.startswith(\"V5_\") or _ob.parent is not None:\r\n1205:         continue\r\n1206:     if not _ob.data.vertices:\r\n1207:         continue\r\n1208:     _mb = _ob.matrix_basis\r\n1209:     if any(abs(_mb[i][j] - _I4[i][j]) > 1e-9 for i in range(4) for j in range(4)):\r\n1210:         continue                                   # 已有自身变换 = 已以几何中心为原点\r\n1211:     _xs = [_v.co.x for _v in _ob.data.vertices]\r\n1212:     _ys = [_v.co.y for _v in _ob.data.vertices]\r\n1213:     _zs = [_v.co.z for _v in _ob.data.vertices]\r\n1214:     _c = Vector(((min(_xs) + max(_xs)) / 2, (min(_ys) + max(_ys)) / 2, (min(_zs) + max(_zs)) / 2))\r\n1215:     _ob.data.transform(Matrix.Translation(-_c))\r\n1216:     _ob.data.update()\r\n1217:     _ob.location = _c\r\n1218:     _moved += 1\r\n1219: bpy.context.view_layer.update()\r\n1220: \r\n1221: # 13b. 组件 Empty 父子：保持世界变换（child.matrix_basis = parent⁻¹ · child_world，parent_inverse = I），\r\n1222: #      这样子物体的 location 直接读作\"相对组件中心\"的坐标，移动/旋转 Empty 整个组件跟着走。\r\n1223: _parented = 0\r\n1224: for _em, _parts in ASSEMBLIES:\r\n1225:     _inv = _em.matrix_basis.inverted()\r\n1226:     for _ob in _parts:\r\n1227:         _mw = _ob.matrix_basis.copy()             # 未挂父时 matrix_basis == 世界变换\r\n1228:         _ob.parent = _em\r\n1229:         _ob.matrix_parent_inverse = Matrix.Identity(4)\r\n1230:         _ob.matrix_basis = _inv @ _mw\r\n1231:         _parented += 1\r\n1232: bpy.context.view_layer.update()\r\n1233: print(\"assemblies: %d empties, %d parented parts\" % (len(ASSEMBLIES), _parented))\r\n1234: \r\n1235: _root = scene.collection\r\n1236: _cols = {}\r\n1237: for _g in _GROUPS:\r\n1238:     _cc = bpy.data.collections.get(_g) or bpy.data.collections.new(_g)\r\n1239:     if _cc.name not in _root.children:\r\n1240:         _root.children.link(_cc)\r\n1241:     _cols[_g] = _cc\r\n1242: \r\n1243: \r\n1244: def _bucket(nm):\r\n1245:     for _g, _ps in _GROUPS.items():\r\n1246:         for _p in _ps:\r\n1247:             if nm.startswith(_p):\r\n1248:                 return _g\r\n1249:     return None\r\n1250: \r\n1251: \r\n1252: _reg = 0\r\n1253: for _ob in list(bpy.data.objects):\r\n1254:     _g = _bucket(_ob.name)\r\n1255:     if not _g:\r\n1256:         continue\r\n1257:     for _c in list(_ob.users_collection):\r\n1258:         _c.objects.unlink(_ob)\r\n1259:     _cols[_g].objects.link(_ob)\r\n1260:     _reg += 1\r\n1261: print(\"organize: origin_to_geometry=%d  regrouped=%d\" % (_moved, _reg))\r\n1262: \r\n1263: # 13c. 清掉空的杂乱集合（v4 遗留：09_Studio_Stage_Rig、WheelSpokes_*，都是 0 对象 0 子集合）\r\n1264: _dropped = []\r\n1265: for _c in list(bpy.data.collections):\r\n1266:     if (_c.name == \"09_Studio_Stage_Rig\" or _c.name.startswith(\"WheelSpokes_\")) \\\r\n1267:             and len(_c.all_objects) == 0 and len(_c.children) == 0:\r\n1268:         _dropped.append(_c.name)\r\n1269:         bpy.data.collections.remove(_c)\r\n1270: print(\"removed empty collections:\", _dropped)\r\n1271: print(\"FINAL objects:\", len(bpy.data.objects),\r\n1272:       \"| V5 meshes:\", sum(1 for o in bpy.data.objects if o.type == 'MESH' and o.name.startswith(\"V5_\")),\r\n1273:       \"| empties:\", sum(1 for o in bpy.data.objects if o.type == 'EMPTY'))\r\n1274: \r\n1275: bpy.ops.wm.save_as_mainfile(filepath=OUT)\r\n1276: print(\"ENV SAVED:\", OUT)\r"}
{"step_index":30,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-18T05:22:53Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-18T13:22:53+08:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-18T13:22:53+08:00\nShowing lines 620-696 of 696\n620: scene.render.use_motion_blur = True\r\n621: scene.render.motion_blur_shutter = 0.17\r\n622: scene.render.motion_blur_position = 'CENTER'\r\n623: scene.render.image_settings.file_format = 'JPEG'\r\n624: scene.render.image_settings.quality = 95\r\n625: scene.render.filepath = os.path.join(FRAMES_DIR, \"f_\")\r\n626: scene.view_settings.view_transform = 'AgX'\r\n627: for look in ('High Contrast', 'AgX - High Contrast', 'Medium High Contrast'):\r\n628:     try:\r\n629:         scene.view_settings.look = look\r\n630:         break\r\n631:     except Exception:\r\n632:         continue\r\n633: scene.view_settings.exposure = 0.50\r\n634: scene.view_settings.gamma = 1.0\r\n635: \r\n636: # 泛光\r\n637: try:\r\n638:     ng = bpy.data.node_groups.new(\"Comp_V5\", 'CompositorNodeTree')\r\n639:     rl = ng.nodes.new(\"CompositorNodeRLayers\")\r\n640:     glare = ng.nodes.new(\"CompositorNodeGlare\")\r\n641:     for val in (\"Bloom\", \"BLOOM\", \"bloom\"):\r\n642:         try:\r\n643:             glare.inputs['Type'].default_value = val\r\n644:             break\r\n645:         except Exception:\r\n646:             continue\r\n647:     for nm, v in ((\"Threshold\", 2.0), (\"Strength\", 0.16), (\"Size\", 6)):\r\n648:         if nm in glare.inputs:\r\n649:             try:\r\n650:                 glare.inputs[nm].default_value = v\r\n651:             except Exception:\r\n652:                 pass\r\n653:     try:\r\n654:         comp = ng.nodes.new(\"CompositorNodeComposite\")\r\n655:     except Exception:\r\n656:         comp = ng.nodes.new(\"NodeGroupOutput\")\r\n657:         if not any(s.name == \"Image\" for s in ng.interface.items_tree):\r\n658:             ng.interface.new_socket(name=\"Image\", in_out='OUTPUT', socket_type='NodeSocketColor')\r\n659:     ng.links.new(rl.outputs['Image'], glare.inputs['Image'])\r\n660:     ng.links.new(glare.outputs['Image'], comp.inputs['Image'])\r\n661:     scene.compositing_node_group = ng\r\n662:     scene.use_nodes = True\r\n663:     print(\"COMPOSITOR OK\")\r\n664: except Exception as e:\r\n665:     print(\"COMPOSITOR FAILED:\", e)\r\n666: \r\n667: bpy.ops.wm.save_as_mainfile(filepath=OUT)\r\n668: print(\"ANIM SAVED:\", OUT)\r\n669: \r\n670: # ---------------------------------------------------------------\r\n671: # 7. 测试渲染\r\n672: # ---------------------------------------------------------------\r\n673: def render_frames(frames, outdir, res=1280, samples=24):\r\n674:     os.makedirs(outdir, exist_ok=True)\r\n675:     scene.render.resolution_x = res\r\n676:     scene.render.resolution_y = int(res * 9 / 16)\r\n677:     scene.eevee.taa_render_samples = samples\r\n678:     for f in frames:\r\n679:         scene.frame_set(f)\r\n680:         scene.render.filepath = os.path.join(outdir, f\"test_{f:04d}.jpg\")\r\n681:         bpy.ops.render.render(write_still=True)\r\n682:         print(\"TEST FRAME\", f)\r\n683: \r\n684: \r\n685: test = argval(\"--test\")\r\n686: if test:\r\n687:     render_frames([int(x) for x in str(test).split(\",\")], os.path.join(PROJ, \"renders_v5\", \"test\"),\r\n688:                   res=1600, samples=24)\r\n689: \r\n690: if argval(\"--render\"):\r\n691:     os.makedirs(FRAMES_DIR, exist_ok=True)\r\n692:     scene.render.resolution_x = 1920\r\n693:     scene.render.resolution_y = 1080\r\n694:     scene.render.filepath = os.path.join(FRAMES_DIR, \"f_\")\r\n695:     bpy.ops.render.render(animation=True)\r\n696:     print(\"RENDER DONE\")\r"}
{"step_index":31,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-18T05:22:53Z","input_tokens":8074,"cache_read_tokens":54217,"output_tokens":12253,"thinking":"The `v5_env.py` script reveals the recent addition of \"Empty\" parents, potentially using the `EM_Stand_*` prefix. This suggests a change in how assemblies are organized within the environment. Further investigation is required to determine the exact prefix for the new empties and how they are used. The use of Empties usually indicates a change in how the objects within the environment are placed in a hierarchy.\n\n\nThe `_GROUPS` Empties might be integrated, or possibly outside the expected `V5_04_Stands` / `V5_06_Props` hierarchies. The `v5_viewport_fast.py` script, pre-dating mesh merging and Empty assemblies, needs validation for compatibility. The `v5_clay.py` script's car check, using `GEO_Race`, raises a potential conflict: is `GEO_Race` part of the cars or legacy track? Running `verifier` and `anim` checks seems necessary. The clay render frames completed, but the muxing script hasn't run yet. Finally, it should be clarified whether `brake_heat` only affects the rear tail light.\n\n\nInitial concern centers on cameras and audio. Camera DoF, obstruction, and steering wheel animation are under review for broadcast realism. Audio analysis indicates the need for engine sound integration via RPM, turbo, and gearshift effects, which can be implemented using ffmpeg and Python to create silent videos and extract stills.\n\n\nThe audio pipeline generates a 90-second F1 soundscape using track data and animation information, incorporating engine sounds, gear changes, and Doppler effects, then mixes this with the existing music. The system's design is reviewed to ensure there are no file collisions, and clear handoffs between the 4 workers and monitor.\n\n\nInspecting the latest Blender files for environment issues, animation problems, and potential API deprecations, focusing on collections and `EM_*` objects. Visual inspection of rendered clay and regular frames highlights potential visual defects in terms of lighting and framing. Audit findings will be tagged for appropriate teams based on the issue.\n\n\nFocusing on the final verification process after environment, animation, and sound effects report completion. It involves comprehensive checks: physics integrity, camera obstructions, collection structure, script functionality, and visual inspection of rendered stills. This also includes audio and video duration, stream verification, loudness analysis, and ensuring documentation consistency before flagging issues directly to involved teams or coordinating if all tests pass. This confirms that track environment, car materials, and lighting author are responsible for specific files related to the track environment, textures, and the environment blend file, but not animation, clay rendering, stills generation, or viewport scripts.\n\n\nFocusing on the Blender file updates and related scripts to organize scene elements under assembly Empties and integrate environment details. The goal is to ensure a clean hierarchy within the Outliner, eliminate orphaned assets, and enhance track realism through procedural textures and refinements. Specific tasks include fixing the scene hierarchy, adding procedural details for track surfaces, and refining kerb profiles and trackside assets.\n\n\nExamining the F1 car shaders in `v4_stage_rig.blend`, particularly carbon fiber, paint, and tire materials, to ensure they're correctly processed by `v5_env.py` and light-linking remains intact. Refining sky and lighting: smoothing horizon haze, refining multi-band sky dome, enhancing sun highlights, and ensuring trackside floodlights render effectively at dusk.\n\nRunning `v5_env.py` with Blender and verifying build time and object count remain optimized. Generating preview stills for visual inspection and summarizing findings for handoff to `@anim` for `v5_stage_anim.blend` and `v5_stage_anim_clay.blend` updates.\n\n\nCamera obstructions and framing require focused attention across the 26 shots, particularly concerning occlusion or clipping issues with environmental elements. The `v5_anim.py` script needs updating to incorporate fixes for camera obstructions and refine camera banking and roll. The Blender files for both animation and clay renders require direct modification for camera and animation updates.\n\n\nFocusing on visual realism in the shots, the plan is to implement subtle camera micro-shake based on car speed and enable realistic depth of field for telephoto and macro shots. Dynamic car feedback will also be added, including brake disc glow, a pulsing rear tail light, and steering wheel rotation in the onboard views, dependent on mesh/bone presence. Finally, ensuring the Blender compositor effects and clay/viewport tools continue to function correctly is important.\n\n\nInvestigating updates to several scripts: `v5_env.py` for correct Empty/object classification, and `v5_viewport_fast.py` to support new assemblies and meshes. Upgrading `v5_stills.py` to render all 26 stills directly from the animation blend file and create an annotated contact sheet.\n\nThe workflow involves testing against the current environment blend file, then re-running animation and clay rendering after `@env` finalizes it. Rendering includes 26 stills and 6 clay comparison stills, avoiding overwrite of existing clay frames. Finally, updating documentation to include all swarm improvements.\n\n\nThe clay video muxing stalled despite frame completion; the cause requires investigation, possibly file path issues. The focus is now on ensuring the telemetry-driven F1 hybrid audio synthesis and correct audio mixing with the silent clay video. After successful muxing and audio mixing, the `@verifier` team will be notified to review the final composite.\n\n\nThe clay video muxing stalled because the dated outputs, `f1_silverstone_clay_1080p.mp4` and `f1_silverstone_clay_silent.mp4`, hadn't been regenerated.  Generating new versions of those videos and a clay contact sheet is the current priority.  The engine sound synthesis pipeline will use track data and camera schedules to generate a 90-second audio track.  This pipeline will read data for track elements and camera parameters to render a realistic F1 hybrid audio track.\n\n\nFocusing on realistic F1 engine audio using Python, defining gear ratios, throttle/load response, and ignition cut sounds. The soundscape requires multi-harmonic exhaust, turbo whine, DRS wind, and kerb rumble effects based on camera position and shot type. Implementing camera-aware spatial acoustics, stereo panning, Doppler shift, and inverse-distance attenuation to create immersive soundscapes for varying camera angles.\n\n\nGenerating silent and SFX-mixed video variants, updating mux scripts to produce both. Adding `synth_sfx.py` and new video outputs to documentation for animation and verification teams. Evaluating a potential protocol violation, specifically whether multiple swarm actions can be called simultaneously.\n\n\nAnalyzing swarm actions, specifically the `add` calls, checking against documented guidelines. Confirmed `model` should be omitted from `add` to force all workers to use the default model. The workspace parameter is unnecessary because the working directory is not a repository. The `brief` parameter must ensure strict file ownership and only mention the next peer.\n\n\nThe initial swarm creation requires all workers to be added in a single turn without immediate follow-up actions. Workers should be briefed to post to their next peer, or the coordinator if at the end of their pipeline, to ensure correct wakeup. Double-checking the handoff graph is crucial to prevent deadlocks or missed wakeups, specifically for the first round of audit by `@verifier`. The `sfx` worker will run independently after being added to the swarm.\n\n\nFocusing on ensuring the correct execution order of tasks between different workers. The sound effects worker (`sfx`) is responsible for generating audio and video outputs, and then notifying the animation and verification teams. The environment worker (`env`) upgrades the environment and renders preview stills before reporting to the animation team. The animation worker (`anim`) requires integration of work done by both the environment and sound effect workers and must ensure that it's finished the initial work before those steps are completed.\n\n\n`anim`'s workflow is now clearly defined: `anim` runs only after `@env` saves the final environment blend and `@sfx` posts audio paths.  `anim` then runs `v5_anim.py` and `v5_clay.py`, renders stills and performs roundtrip viewport tests. Finally, updates documentation and notifies `@verifier`. The `@verifier` team is now confirmed to begin when `@anim` and `@sfx` hand off after running their tasks, they can perform QA.\n\n\nVerification passed, tagging the coordinator with complete QA sign-off. Rethinking the handoff: ensuring sound effects finish *before* animation's final documentation pass is critical. The animation worker will now check for the environment blend file before building the animation blend files and stills, notifying the verifier for visual QA and updating documentation when sound effects are available. Now proceeding with swarm calls. Investigating the `swarm{action:\"title\"}` call order; determining if it must precede, follow, or run in parallel with the `add` calls. Reviewing `swarm` tool description for clarification.\n\n\nThe `add` action immediately follows the `title` action according to the workflow instructions, so calling `add` now should be safe. Step 5 suggests ending the turn immediately after `add`, and without any explicit follow-up instructions. Calling title, adding all workers, and ending the turn seems to be the correct, initial swarm setup.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"swarm","args":{"action":"title","title":"blender-supercar V5 场景/镜头/音效全链路优化"}},{"name":"swarm","args":{"action":"add","brief":"You are the QA & Visual/Technical Verifier for `D:\\项目session\\blender-supercar` (Blender 5.3.0 headless `/d/APPs/steam/steamapps/common/Blender/blender.exe`, pure CPU EEVEE, ffmpeg `/c/Users/86052/scoop/shims/ffmpeg.exe`).\n\nSTRICT OWNERSHIP & BOUNDARIES:\n- You are READ-ONLY on all project files (`pipeline/`, `LATEST/`, `textures/`, `renders_v5/`, `docs/`, `README.md`). Never edit project files or overwrite `.blend` / render outputs.\n- Put any temporary diagnostic Python scripts or scratch images ONLY in `C:\\Users\\86052\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\1a8ac0b5-f848-4c0e-bc45-8abba2abb2e8\\scratch\\`.\n- Mention discipline: `@name` is a wakeup doorbell, never a CC. Tag ONLY the worker(s) who need to act next (`@env`, `@anim`, `@sfx`), and tag `@coordinator` ONLY when final Round 2 verification passes or on a hard blocker.\n\nYOUR TWO-PHASE MISSION:\n1) ROUND 1 — Immediate Baseline Audit (start right now):\n   - Run a headless read-only Blender inspection script on `LATEST/v5_stage_anim.blend` and `LATEST/v5_stage_anim_clay.blend` to check:\n     a) Outliner hygiene: are any `EM_*` assembly Empties or V5/V4 objects stranded in root `Scene Collection` instead of `V5_01_Road`..`V5_07_Lighting`? Any orphan meshes, broken material links, missing textures, or misclassified car vs env meshes in `v5_clay.py` (check `GEO_Race*` vs car parts)? Does `v5_viewport_fast.py` cover the new Empty assemblies & merged meshes?\n     b) Camera-to-car line-of-sight across ALL 26 shots (frames 1..2161, step 4): raycast from active camera to car (`Bone_Root` world position + 0.5m Z) in `LATEST/v5_stage_anim.blend` and list any shots/frames occluded by bridges, stands, barriers, brake boards, or pit walls, plus any camera frustum clipping or ground penetration (`cam.z < 0.15`).\n     c) Car shader / rig inspection: list car meshes/materials (brake discs/rotors, tail light, steering wheel, decals, tires, body paint) so `@env` and `@anim` know exact object/material/bone names for upgrades (brake disc heat glow, steering wheel rotation, DOF target, carbon/paint polish).\n   - Visually inspect representative frames from the newly rendered `renders_v5/clay_frames/` (e.g. build a scratch contact sheet and view with `read_file`) and existing `renders_v5/frames/` / `renders_v5/stills/` to spot concrete visual flaws (sky banding, flat braking zones, lighting/exposure issues, awkward framing, z-fighting).\n   - Post ONE structured Round 1 audit report tagging `@env` and `@anim` with exact object names, frame numbers, and prioritized fixes.\n\n2) ROUND 2 — Final Deliverable Verification (after `@anim` and `@sfx` report completion):\n   - Re-run your headless Blender audit on rebuilt `LATEST/v5_stage_env.blend`, `LATEST/v5_stage_anim.blend`, and `LATEST/v5_stage_anim_clay.blend`: verify 0 physics violations, 0 unintended camera obstructions, clean Outliner collections, working `v5_viewport_fast.py`, and single-frame 1080p render speed stays reasonable (~2-3.5s CPU).\n   - Visually inspect the newly rendered 26-shot color stills (`renders_v5/stills/contact_sheet.jpg` + individual `shot_*.jpg`) and clay test stills (`renders_v5/clay_stills/`) via `read_file` to confirm high visual quality, DOF, brake glow, sky/lighting, and track details.\n   - Verify `@sfx`'s outputs (`f1_silverstone_clay_1080p.mp4`, `sfx_engine_90s.wav`, `audio_v5_sfx_mix_90s.m4a`, `f1_silverstone_clay_sfx_1080p.mp4`, `f1_silverstone_lap_sfx_1080p.mp4`) via `ffprobe` / `ffmpeg` loudness check (duration ~90.0s, valid streams, no clipping/NaNs, smooth audio).\n   - Check `README.md`, `LATEST/README.txt`, and `docs/README_V5.md` match actual files and scripts.\n   - If issues remain, tag ONLY the responsible author (`@env`, `@anim`, or `@sfx`). When everything passes, post a concise verification summary tagging `@coordinator`.","name":"verifier"}},{"name":"swarm","args":{"action":"add","brief":"You are the Environment, 