inator` only if blocked.\n\nMISSION — Fix Stale Clay Mux & Build Telemetry-Driven F1 V6 Hybrid Audio Layer:\n1) Immediate Clay Mux Refresh:\n   - `renders_v5/clay_frames/f_0001.jpg`..`f_2161.jpg` finished rendering today at 13:19, while `f1_silverstone_clay_silent.mp4` and `f1_silverstone_clay_1080p.mp4` are stale from yesterday.\n   - Run `ffmpeg` to encode fresh `renders_v5/f1_silverstone_clay_silent.mp4` and `renders_v5/f1_silverstone_clay_1080p.mp4` (24 fps, libx264 `-crf 18`, `+faststart`), and generate an updated 26-shot clay contact sheet `renders_v5/clay_stills/contact_sheet_clay.jpg` from `clay_frames`.\n2) Telemetry-Synced F1 V6 Turbo-Hybrid Audio Synthesizer (`pipeline/synth_sfx.py`):\n   - Solve the major missing feature noted in `docs/README_V5.md` §8 (\"没有引擎声：片子只有配乐。要加需要 RPM/涡轮/换挡音效层，按 gear 和时间轴对齐\").\n   - Read `track_data/silverstone_track.json` (`t`, `v_mps`, `curv_1pm`, `s`, `racing_xy`) and read the 26-shot timeline & camera positions/types from `pipeline/v5_anim.py` (read-only) so the audio matches the exact 2161 frames (`FPS=24`, total `2161/24 = 90.0417 s`, time mapping `t_sim = f_idx * (LAP_S / 2160)`).\n   - Synthesize `renders_v5/sfx_engine_90s.wav` (48 kHz, 16-bit stereo WAV) using Python (`numpy`/`scipy` if installed, or fast vectorized Python/math):\n     * Realistic 8-speed F1 gearbox curve (shifts across ~80..331 km/h, keeping RPM in the authentic 9,800–12,600 RPM powerband), throttle load driven by longitudinal acceleration `dv/dt`;\n     * Rich F1 1.6L V6 hybrid timbre: fundamental `RPM/60 * 3` Hz + odd/even exhaust harmonics + formant/bandpass resonator (no harsh pure-sine buzz!) + MGU-H turbo whistle (~2.5–5.5 kHz subtle sheen) + crisp ~45 ms upshift ignition-cut pop + rapid downshift rev-match throttle blips under braking;\n     * High-speed aerodynamic wind rush (`~ v^2`), subtle kerb rumble vibration when cornering hard (`|curv| > 0.008`), and **camera-perspective acoustic modeling** across all 26 shots:\n       - `Onboard` (`S02